I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `StateHandle<'seen', read>`, so it has no authority to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or to call `metadata.internal.example`. Adding either would mean importing an interface the graph never granted. The target also has no WASI adapter, so there is no filesystem to write to. The metadata call would additionally send each item's text to an external service, which changes the node's data flow. Operations should raise these with the graph owner. Logging could go in a node that holds a write capability or be done host-side, and enrichment would need an explicit `http-client` grant with a host allowlist.

